# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default. A shell script
# with CRLF fails under bash with "$'\r': command not found", and a container
# that mounts a script or config written on Windows sees the same stray \r.
# Everything in the index is LF; these rules keep the scripts and the files the
# containers read LF in every working tree, whatever core.autocrlf says.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ndjson text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
